</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Most loaded tools remain unused.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The agent is shown 23 tool schemas on every turn, yet no repository invokes more than 7 (<a href="#S2.F3.sf2" title="In Fig. 3 ‣ Operational work repeats within a repository. ‣ 2.2 Three Sources of Removable Cost ‣ 2 Cost Profiling and Analysis of Fixed Cost-control Strategies ‣ TokenEconomizer: Experience-Driven Black-Box Cost Control for Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(b)</span></a>). Of these tools, 16 are never called and 3 account for 98% of all calls; the remaining tools are sparsely and unevenly used across repositories. A fixed reduced interface could therefore remove shared overhead but also suppress a locally useful tool, motivating evidence-based pruning that can recover a pruned tool.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Failed trajectories consume disproportionate cost.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The 10 failed executions constitute 17% of the tasks but 32% of total spend (<a href="#S2.F3.sf3" title="In Fig. 3 ‣ Operational work repeats within a repository. ‣ 2.2 Three Sources of Removable Cost ‣ 2 Cost Profiling and Analysis of Fixed Cost-control Strategies ‣ TokenEconomizer: Experience-Driven Black-Box Cost Control for Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(c)</span></a>). A universal turn limit cannot identify them: Matplotlib failures are much longer than successful runs (45 versus 20 turns), whereas Sphinx failures run only slightly longer than its successful runs (36 versus 31). In total, 45 trajectories repeat an earlier failure signature, the normalized first error line of a failing output (<a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Additional Meta-strategy Details ‣ TokenEconomizer: Experience-Driven Black-Box Cost Control for Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>), and 51% of the 60 tasks’ spend falls after a trajectory’s first repetition. Repetition alone does not mark failure, however: 36 of the 50 successful runs also repeat a signature, and more than half of the spend after a repetition falls in runs that go on to succeed. A guard must therefore separate persistent loops from recoverable ones, for instance by comparing a run’s length with the repository’s successful runs, and should redirect before it terminates.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Together, these observations motivate three adaptive decisions, which <a href="#S3" title="3 TokenEconomizer ‣ TokenEconomizer: Experience-Driven Black-Box Cost Control for Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> implements as meta-strategies whose policies are learned separately within each environment: which operational knowledge to inject, which persistently irrelevant tools to prune, and when to intervene in an unproductive failure loop.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span><span id="S3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">TokenEconomizer</span></h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce <span id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">TokenEconomizer</span>, an external controller that applies three repository-agnostic meta-strategies to learn repository-specific policies from completed traces. Without modifying the underlying agent, it acts through the instruction prefix, loaded tools, and live event stream to synthesize and selectively activate operational micro-skills, prune unnecessary tools, and intervene in unproductive failure loops (<a href="#S3.F4" title="In 3 TokenEconomizer ‣ TokenEconomizer: Experience-Driven Black-Box Cost Control for Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). Throughout, a <em id="S3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">meta-strategy</em> is one of these three environment-agnostic procedures, a <em id="S3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">policy</em> is the environment-specific decision it learns, and a <em id="S3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">fixed strategy</em>, such as RTK or RepoMap, applies one configuration in every environment.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our unit of optimization is a chronological task stream <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> within an environment. By default, an agent runs task <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> under an instruction prefix <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the harness’s system instructions followed by the description of <math id="S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, with every tool in the harness’s catalog loaded. When the controller is active, it maintains repository state <math id="S3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which records the micro-skills and supporting evidence, tool-use history, and turn statistics accumulated from the completed tasks <math id="S3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{i-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{i-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> empty. Before <math id="S3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> starts, the controller <math id="S3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> determines the set of active policies based on the task description and current state:</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta P_{i},\mathcal{U}_{i},B_{i})=\mathcal{C}(\tau_{i},S_{i-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta P_{i},\mathcal{U}_{i},B_{i})=\mathcal{C}(\tau_{i},S_{i-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
