<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The policies given by <math id="S3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> are the set <math id="S3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of micro-skills activated at task <math id="S3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, which depends only on <math id="S3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and is rendered as a short manual inserted into <math id="S3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> between the harness instructions and the task description; the loaded tool set <math id="S3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, restricted to catalog tools that remain plausibly useful; and a turn budget <math id="S3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> that calibrates when an in-flight failure-loop guard may redirect or terminate the rollout. The agent then runs <math id="S3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> under these policies, producing a trajectory <math id="S3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, from which the controller updates the repository state to <math id="S3.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. The controller may also leave the agent’s default configuration in place by activating no micro-skills, keeping the full tool catalog loaded, or never intervening. Its objective is to minimize mean per-task cost, including its own calls, while keeping success near default execution (<a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Task Stream Formulation and Cost Accounting ‣ TokenEconomizer: Experience-Driven Black-Box Cost Control for Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>, <a href="#A5.E6" title="In Cost attribution and objective. ‣ Appendix E Task Stream Formulation and Cost Accounting ‣ TokenEconomizer: Experience-Driven Black-Box Cost Control for Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).</p>
</div>
