<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Conceptually, <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">TokenEconomizer</span> seeks to reduce amortized cost while preserving the success of default execution:</p>
<table id="A5.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\mathcal{C}}\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\overline{C}_{r}(\mathcal{C})\right]\quad\text{subject to}\quad\mathbb{E}\!\left[\overline{Y}_{r}(\mathcal{C})\right]\geq\mathbb{E}\!\left[\overline{Y}_{r}(\mathrm{default})\right]-\epsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.447em">⁡</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>subject to</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>default</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\mathcal{C}}\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\overline{C}_{r}(\mathcal{C})\right]\quad\text{subject to}\quad\mathbb{E}\!\left[\overline{Y}_{r}(\mathcal{C})\right]\geq\mathbb{E}\!\left[\overline{Y}_{r}(\mathrm{default})\right]-\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">The expectation is over stochastic agent execution. <a href="#A5.E6" title="In Cost attribution and objective. ‣ Appendix E Task Stream Formulation and Cost Accounting ‣ TokenEconomizer: Experience-Driven Black-Box Cost Control for Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> states the design objective rather than an evaluation-time tuning rule: we do not select <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> after observing the results. Instead, experiments report the observed cost change and success difference relative to matched default executions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">At finalization, task-agent usage and all attributed controller calls are written to the same execution record before <a href="#A5.E4" title="In Cost attribution and objective. ‣ Appendix E Task Stream Formulation and Cost Accounting ‣ TokenEconomizer: Experience-Driven Black-Box Cost Control for Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> is evaluated. This shared accounting path prevents an optimized method from omitting work moved into an auxiliary call or obtaining an unreported discount through different model routing.</p>
</div>
</section>
