<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Additional Meta-strategy Details</h2>

<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Micro-skill injection.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proposer is called after task 4 and every 5 tasks thereafter. Each call sees digests of the repository’s 8 most recent tasks, which contain no solution text or gold patches, and returns at most 4 candidates. A candidate is discarded unless it cites at least 2 tasks in the window on which its confirming detector matches. An admitted candidate’s detectors are run retroactively over the window’s tasks, so it enters with their evidence and can be activated at once. On an exercised task, contradiction is checked before confirmation, and a skill without a need detector counts every exercised task as needed. A skill the proposer marks as high-stakes, such as a test command or a build step, retires at its first contradiction once it has met the confirmation condition. <a href="#A6.T5" title="In Micro-skill injection. ‣ Appendix F Additional Meta-strategy Details ‣ TokenEconomizer: Experience-Driven Black-Box Cost Control for Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> summarizes the lifecycle. The three criteria act at different points: the confirmation count moves a candidate to confirmed, the need rate decides on each task whether a confirmed skill is injected, and the support <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}(f)</annotation></semantics></math> decides retirement. Support is checked only once a skill is confirmed, so a candidate with negative support, which is never injected, stays a candidate; if it is later confirmed, it retires after the next task unless its support has turned positive.</p>
</div>
