<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Ablations of Meta-strategies</h2>

<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each single-meta-strategy variant uses the same parameters as the full stack (<a href="#A3.T4" title="In Appendix C Controller Configuration ‣ TokenEconomizer: Experience-Driven Black-Box Cost Control for Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), so no variant is tuned for its own ablation. <a href="#S4.T2.st1" title="In Table 2 ‣ 4.3 Generalization to Diverse Task Structures ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ TokenEconomizer: Experience-Driven Black-Box Cost Control for Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2(a)</span></a> reports the cost and Pass@1 of each variant, paired against default execution over the same task–seed units as <a href="#S4.T1" title="In 4.2 SWE-Bench Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ TokenEconomizer: Experience-Driven Black-Box Cost Control for Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. <a href="#A8.T6" title="In Appendix H Ablations of Meta-strategies ‣ TokenEconomizer: Experience-Driven Black-Box Cost Control for Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> reports how often each meta-strategy acted, and <a href="#A8.T7" title="In Appendix H Ablations of Meta-strategies ‣ TokenEconomizer: Experience-Driven Black-Box Cost Control for Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> defines its columns. All columns are per-stream means, but their units differ. <em id="A8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Needed</em> counts events, one for each exercised task that needed a skill, and is therefore 33 to 37 times the number of confirmed skills beside it. <em id="A8.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Masked</em> is the number of tools still masked at the end of a stream, whereas <em id="A8.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Re-audits</em> counts tasks run with the full catalog, so the two are not comparable. Meta-strategies that a variant disables are reported as zero.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Within each setting, the counts of the combined stack remain close to those of the corresponding single-meta-strategy variant, which indicates that the three meta-strategies seldom interfere with one another’s decisions. The counts also show how selectively each meta-strategy acts. About one in five proposed skills is retired within its stream, so the ledger revises its beliefs rather than accumulating them. The trace judge is consulted about 10 to 13 times per stream, but redirects follow on roughly one task in ten and aborts on fewer than one in twenty, since most escalations end in a productive or uncertain verdict.</p>
</div>
