<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Examples of Meta-strategy Decisions</h2>

<div id="A9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix illustrates each meta-strategy with examples from SWE-Bench: micro-skills in (a)–(e), tool masks in (f) and (g), and failure-loop interventions in (h) and (i). Examples (a), (b), and (f)–(i) compare <span id="A9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">TokenEconomizer</span> with default execution on the same task.</p>
</div>
<section id="A9.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.1 </span>Micro-skill Injection</h3>

<div id="A9.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each micro-skill example gives the skill as injected, its detectors as the proposer wrote them, and its lifecycle in the stream that learned it. Examples (a) and (b) are activated and injected, and each ends with one task that received the skill, compared with default execution. The remaining three illustrate the other outcomes: (c) is retired by a contradiction, (d) is confirmed but never clears the need gate, and (e) never meets the confirmation condition.</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Tasks are numbered by their position in the stream, so the proposer runs after tasks 4, 9, 14, and so on. A detector is a regular expression over the task’s commands and outputs unless it names a built-in predicate, such as <span id="A9.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ran_tests</span>, or an extractor the proposer defined, whose pattern is given in parentheses; a dash marks a detector the proposer omitted. In the traces, each line that starts with <span id="A9.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">$</span> or a tool name such as <span id="A9.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Edit</span> is one tool call, indented grey text is its output, and a grey count in parentheses stands for tool calls that are not shown.</p>
</div>
