<div id="A9.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The instruction is wrong for this environment, which has no pytest: all 57 traces in the stream that invoke pytest fail with <span id="A9.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">No module named pytest</span>. The skill was nonetheless activated, because its confirming detector matches the pytest command itself rather than a passing result, so the agent’s failed attempts on tasks 2–5 counted as confirmations. The first task to receive the skill tried the command and then probed for the module, and the probe’s <span id="A9.SS1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ModuleNotFoundError</span> matched the contradicting detector. Weighted by <math id="A9.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=5</annotation></semantics></math>, that single contradiction outweighs the decayed confirmations, and the skill left the manual after one injection. Example (a) shows the native runner that another stream learned for the same repository.</p>
</div>
