<section id="A10" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix J </span>Harness-specific Customization</h2>

<div id="A10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">TokenEconomizer</span> reaches each agent only through interfaces its harness already exposes: the task prompt, the tool configuration applied at launch, and the event stream the harness emits while it runs. The three meta-strategies and normalized trace format are shared across harnesses, and harness-specific adapters implement the available controls. Every paid controller call uses the same model and routing as the task agent.</p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Vendor-specific event streams are converted into a common representation containing tool names, arguments, observations, model outputs, usage, and grading outcomes. Meta-strategy implementations consume only this normalized interface. All experiments use Claude Code 2.1.170, Codex 0.153.1, and GitHub Copilot CLI 1.0.84-7.</p>
</div>
<section id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Answer-key guard.</h4>

<div id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Web-Bench grading specifications and SWE-Bench fix commits are public on GitHub, so an agent with network access could read the answer instead of solving the task. On both benchmarks, every method, including default execution, therefore runs behind the same guard on all three harnesses: the task container resolves GitHub hosts to an unreachable address, so any command that looks them up by name fails to connect. Claude Code and Copilot CLI additionally run a pre-execution hook that refuses shell commands referencing GitHub; Codex 0.153.1 accepts a hook configuration but did not invoke it in our tests, likely a limitation of this version, so it relies on the first layer alone.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Claude Code.</h4>

<div id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Claude Code runs headless and emits a JSON event stream, which the controller reads live and keeps as the task’s trace. The tool catalog comes from the stream’s session-start event.</p>
<ul id="A10.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:5mm;">
<li id="A10.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A10.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Micro-skills.</em> The rendered manual is prepended to the task prompt.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A10.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Tool pruning.</em> Masked tools are passed to the CLI’s disallowed-tools option, which removes their schemas from every request.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A10.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Failure-loop intervention.</em> The guard reads the stream as it arrives. To redirect, it stops the CLI and starts a new invocation in the same container, with the redirect in its prompt and the agent’s edits still on disk. A second stuck verdict ends the task. Token usage from both invocations is summed.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Codex.</h4>

<div id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Codex also runs headless with a JSON event stream. It differs from the other two harnesses in one interface: its tools cannot be removed one at a time, because groups of related tools and instructions can only be switched on or off in its configuration file.</p>
<ul id="A10.I2" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:5mm;">
<li id="A10.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A10.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Micro-skills.</em> The rendered manual is prepended to the task prompt, as on Claude Code.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A10.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Tool pruning.</em> The pruning unit is a capability package rather than an individual tool: sub-agent collaboration, goal tracking, image input, bundled skills, and the base prompt’s guidance for interactive chat, which a headless run never uses. The rules of <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Meta-strategy II: Tool Pruning ‣ 3 TokenEconomizer ‣ TokenEconomizer: Experience-Driven Black-Box Cost Control for Coding Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> apply to packages unchanged. The mask is written into each task’s configuration file.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A10.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Failure-loop intervention.</em> As on Claude Code, a redirect starts a new invocation in the same container, and a second stuck verdict ends the task.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Copilot CLI.</h4>

<div id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Copilot CLI’s event stream does not report token usage, so the controller reads usage and the tool catalog from the CLI’s debug log.</p>
<ul id="A10.I3" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:5mm;">
<li id="A10.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A10.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Micro-skills.</em> The rendered manual is prepended to the task prompt, as on Claude Code.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A10.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Tool pruning.</em> Masked tools are passed to the CLI’s excluded-tools option, which removes their schemas from the request; its deny-tool option would only refuse execution while still billing each schema on every turn.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A10.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Failure-loop intervention.</em> As on Claude Code, a redirect starts a new invocation in the same container, and a second stuck verdict ends the task.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
